                    <msContents><!-- describe the intellectual content of an inscription -->
                        <summary>
                            This inscription dated to Śaka 902, in the reign of Taila II, describes a donation to an unnamed deity in the presence of the regional (<foreign>nāḻ-gāmuṇḍa</foreign>) and village administrators, (<foreign>ūr-gāmuṇḍa</foreign>) -- Eṟagāri and Eṟecaṭṭa, respectively.
                            They made the donation having washed the feet of Saṁkayya-bhaṭṭāra. Biṭṭayya was the donor for the Nandi-maṇḍapa.
                        </summary>
                        <!-- offers the possibility to give a summary of the inscription's content -->
                    </msContents>
